From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:13:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] um: let VNC input wake a suspended guest

The Darwin host's keyboard, pointer and touchscreen reach the guest
through uml_vnc_input, whose interrupt was not a wake source.  Once a
Darwin system suspend holds until a wake source fires, a guest that
suspended itself, as Android does when its display goes off, could not
be woken from the host's screen: its input waited in the socket for the
next RTC alarm, and the host dropped what did not fit.

Make the input interrupt a wake source, as the RTC alarm's is, so the
suspend leaves it notifying and its input ends the sleep.  Input that
arrives while a suspend is still being entered reports a wakeup, which
aborts the suspend at the PM core's next check.

The input devices offer no power/wakeup control: a device wakeup
source would add a /sys/class/wakeup entry, which Android's policy
labels one source at a time.
---
 arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c b/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
index 6ad13ee15181776f5cf62ecf149f1eadbbe1fc30..92ba59b6056b1ba7bc1023adca73e01f6242d092 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/input.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/byteorder/generic.h>
 
@@ -78,6 +79,9 @@ static irqreturn_t vnc_input_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 		for (index = 0; index < bytes / sizeof(events[0]); ++index)
 			deliver_event(&events[index]);
 	}
+	/* Input that arrives while a suspend is under way ends it. */
+	if (handled)
+		pm_system_wakeup();
 	return handled ? IRQ_HANDLED : IRQ_NONE;
 }
 
@@ -154,6 +158,14 @@ static int __init vnc_input_init(void)
 		error = input_irq;
 		goto unregister_pointer;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The host's keyboard and screen are the guest's own, so their input
+	 * wakes a suspended guest as a laptop's keyboard does.
+	 */
+	error = irq_set_irq_wake(input_irq, 1);
+	if (error)
+		pr_warn("uml_vnc_input: input cannot wake the guest: %d\n",
+			error);
 	pr_info("uml_vnc_input: registered keyboard and tablet at fd=%d\n",
 		input_fd);
 	return 0;
